{"kind":"artifact","text":"notes/2026-09-10-s2-clarifications.md at exact 2b45d85095453df72e39d86d1da5902ce37302cb on request/s2-clarifications (pushed; one commit over main 86970224), the reporting artifact under promise f605b80a on request 6eee19d1 (b4247e09), the S2 decision-preparation child. New file: the clarification proposal for Hugh.\n\nMatter one, the unreadable short selector. The adopted note names this an S2 proposal item in its own words, so the note quotes that sentence and adopts the refusal rather than dissolving it into a resolver detail. Recommended wording: a selector that must resolve against the projection, a display index or a hash fragment, is refused with the resolver's existing event reference error when no full canonical identifier can be obtained, and that refusal is of the selector rather than a judgement about the record it might have named; a full canonical identifier is not refused, because it is classified without reading any log, and its projection-dependent eligibility is reported as not established. Reusing the existing error means no new error text or refusal category enters the surface. Three alternatives are costed: creating with no record reintroduces the unattributed checkout the stage exists to remove, blocking until the projection is readable disables the tool exactly when a log is being repaired, and resolving from a stale cache turns an unknown into a confident wrong answer.\n\nMatter two, the optional hook. Two facts were observed directly in an isolated temporary repository and both observations are quoted in the note. A linked checkout's hooks resolve through the shared common directory, so installation is repository-wide however the flag reads; and GIT_DIR is set per invocation to the invoking checkout's own directory, unset in the main checkout where the working directory is the tree top. The consequence the adopted wording does not disclose is that a script appending one line from the record it was given would stamp every other checkout with a wrong trailer, which is worse than no trailer because the association reads a trailer as a claim. The recommendation needs no relaxation of the existing contract: a shared script finds the invoking checkout's own record at run time using shell builtins alone, with dir set from GIT_DIR falling back to .git, so nothing is exec'd and no bounded helper or Git read is proposed. Exact replacement wording is given for the second sentence and an added disclosure sentence for the first. Six controls accompany it: the wrong checkout, proven by two checkouts with different records and one shared hook each carrying its own lane; a missing record, silent and untrailered, where the unguarded first draft printed a shell redirection error on every commit in every checkout without one, which is the repository-wide harm the disclosure is about and is why the recommended wording tests readability before reading; a malformed record ignored; a foreign record ignored by genesis; an already stamped message left with exactly one trailer across two amends; and the unchanged existing-hook and hooksPath refusals. No worktreeConfig migration is proposed or needed because nothing here writes Git configuration. The template-only fallback is named with its cost and with the adopted optional-hook outcome that would be deferred, rather than dropped.\n\nThe note separates the two decisions Hugh must make from the three planner has already placed inside S2 as ordinary implementation choices: one configured checkout root serving both creation containment and the existing protection, the lane and record readback through the shared captured read, and where the shared settled-status logic lives. Conditions met: a small concrete clarification covering both matters with recommended wording, alternatives and their costs and bounded controls; interpretations of the existing adoption separated from actual changes to it, with the hook change stated plainly as a change because the adopted sentence says the script is given a record while the recommendation says it finds one; and the S2 implementation commitment dc7f7d11 / 664f3636 preserved and progressing independently. This child owes a reviewable decision artifact and this is it: no source change, no adoption, no hook installed in any working repository, no resident rollout. Notes are outside the documentation set (DocsDir is docs), so no gate covers this page; git diff --check and the whole internal/docset package were run at this head and both pass. First publication at this path.","body":{"branch":"request/s2-clarifications","commit":"2b45d85095453df72e39d86d1da5902ce37302cb","path":"notes/2026-09-10-s2-clarifications.md","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:f605b80aef5ec4e4239d5f4172be303285b1f105 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0169ac61d80658478db25ce500d46d087c06fdde, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:01c4e8b02601b3b35241c2baffd15e16e3e3d09d, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:033ceaa3c91aa563b1cc51c1b776c47c90d59242, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:04075a23bf804a9e61f04055021af9a18d6ee9ca and 140 more"}}